      "contentHash": "42d2f62bb336cf6dacc11acacc03f60babc34b1cb5d7596ce9fdf2346ac48ee5",
      "quote": "\nHere, Rirepresents the orthonormal basis of the ellipsoid’s\nthree axes, and the scale factor Sidefines the size along each\ndirection. By compressing the scale factor along specific axes,\nthe Gaussian ellipsoid can be flattened into planes aligned\nwith those axes. We compress the Gaussian ellipsoid along the\ndirection of the minimum scale factor, effectively flattening the\nellipsoid into a plane closest to its original shape.",
      "location": {
